{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>עצבוני</b> — Most of the commentators said that עצבוני is from the root of קדר, shaped me like the sinews of the body. And they explained ותבלעני as referring to the covering over the internal organs that are concealed. But what seems right to me is that the meaning of ידיך is like 'the hand of YHWH' in הויה." "<b>ועצבוני</b> — According to its plain meaning." "Also <b>ויעשוני</b> — like הנני עושה את כל מעניך, and ועשותם רשעים. Also ותבלעני according to its plain meaning."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Job's verse עצבוני ותבלעני from Job 10:8; קדר is from Job 10:11. The last phrase הויה may be shorthand for a verse cited by its opening word, but no such citation is identifiable with certainty; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:21.170122862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}